Here's a C# program that removes all occurrences of a specific item from an array:

```csharp
using System;
using System.Collections.Generic;

class Program
{
    static void Main()
    {
        // Input array
        List<int> array = new List<int> { 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 2, 3, 4 };

        // Item to remove
        int itemToRemove = 3;

        // Create a new list to store the result
        List<int> result = new List<int>();

        // Iterate through the array
        foreach (int number in array)
        {
            // If the number is not the item to remove, add it to the result
            if (number != itemToRemove)
            {
                result.Add(number);
            }
        }

        // Display the result
        Console.WriteLine("Result array: " + string.Join(", ", result));
    }
}
```

